<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Shun of Liu Song</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">467–479</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Liu Zhun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shun-emperor">Emperor Shun</a> of Liu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>, Liu Zhun, was the last emperor of the Liu Song dynasty, placed on the throne as a child in 477 by the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiao-daocheng">Xiao Daocheng</a>. In 479 Xiao forced him to abdicate and founded the Southern Qi dynasty, and the boy was killed soon afterwards.</p></div>
